# A job run in one of two modes. Each choice is made once, in a place with a name: what a mode means is one table
# (`PLANS`), how a level marks a line another (`MARKS`, read by `Report.line`); where the job comes from is the body of
# `source`; `report` builds its Message by one constructor in either arm. The settings are the route's own value; the
# mode and the level `run` reads from them, each held by its field, are the values it hands on.

route clean.runs.run
step run/source
choice run/source/?1
step run/source/?1/load
step run/source/?1/load/Job()
step run/source/?1/infer
step run/source/?1/infer/Job()
step run/finished
step run/finished/Runner()
step run/finished/Runner.batch
step run/report
choice run/report/?1
step run/report/?1/Report()
step run/report/?1/Report.line
step run/report/?1/Message()
step run/report/?1/Message()#2
step run/report/send

line entry > run call
line Settings·settings > run value                                 # run reads the mode and the level from it

# where the job comes from
line run/source/?1/load/Job() > Job@run/source/?1/load/Job() value
line Job@run/source/?1/load/Job() > run/source/?1/load value
line run/source/?1/load > Job@run/source/?1 value
line run/source/?1/infer/Job() > Job@run/source/?1/infer/Job() value
line Job@run/source/?1/infer/Job() > run/source/?1/infer value
line run/source/?1/infer > Job@run/source/?1 value
line Job@run/source/?1 > run/source value
line run/source > Job·job@run/source value
line Job·job@run/source > run/finished value
line Job·job@run/source > run/report value

# whether it finished: a Runner for the mode, and the mode's timeout
known #new line Mode·mode > run/finished value                     # finished looks up the mode's plan itself
line Mode·mode > run/finished/Runner() value
line run/finished/Runner() > Runner@run/finished/Runner() value
line Runner@run/finished/Runner() > run/finished/Runner.batch value
line run/finished/Runner.batch > run/finished back
line run/finished > _@run/finished value                           # the boolean, handed straight to report
line _@run/finished > run/report value

# the line that says how it went: a Report for the level marks it in one arm, and the marked string goes into the
# Message built around it
line Level·level > run/report/?1/Report() value
line run/report/?1/Report() > Report@run/report/?1 value
line Report@run/report/?1 > run/report/?1/Report.line value
line run/report/?1/Report.line > _@run/report/?1 value
line _@run/report/?1 > run/report/?1/Message() value
known #new line run/report/?1/Message() > Message·message@run/report/?1 value
known #new line run/report/?1/Message()#2 > Message·message@run/report/?1 value
known #new line Message·message@run/report/?1 > run/report/send value
line run/report/send > Screen own
line run/report/send > run/report back
line run/report > run back

home Settings·settings run
home Mode·mode run
home Level·level run
home Job@run/source/?1/load/Job() run/source/?1/load
home Job@run/source/?1/infer/Job() run/source/?1/infer
home Job@run/source/?1 run/source
home Job·job@run/source run
home Runner@run/finished/Runner() run/finished
home _@run/finished run
known #new home Report@run/report/?1 run/report/?1            # Atlas: in report, where its own arrow takes it
home _@run/report/?1 run/report/?1
known #new home Message·message@run/report/?1 run/report

side entry left
side Screen right

# the Message either arm builds is two values: of its type without its name, and of its name without a type
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Message() > Message@run/report/?1 value
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Message()#2 > Message@run/report/?1 value
known #new extra line Message@run/report/?1 > run/report/send value
known #new extra home Message@run/report/?1 run/report
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Message() > _·message@run/report/?1 value
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Message()#2 > _·message@run/report/?1 value
known #new extra line _·message@run/report/?1 > run/report/send value
known #new extra home _·message@run/report/?1 run/report

# a value whose field is read into a call's argument counts as handed to that call
known #new extra line Settings·settings > run/finished value
known #new extra line Settings·settings > run/report value
known #new extra line Job·job@run/source > run/report/?1/Report.line value
known #new extra line Job·job@run/source > run/report/?1/Message()#2 value

# an opened step's own arrow takes what its steps make, though only a step inside takes it
known #new extra line Job·job@run/source > run value
known #new extra line Runner@run/finished/Runner() > run/finished value
known #new extra line Report@run/report/?1 > run/report value
known #new extra line Message@run/report/?1 > run/report value

# a result of no type of the code's handed straight to another step goes back to the caller as well
known #new extra line run/finished > run back
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Report.line > run/report back
